{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed&nbsp;development, by reason of siting, scale, design, and bulk, would be a significant addition within the rear garden of the existing property, where it would sit adjacent to several other rear gardens. This&nbsp;would be at odds with the surrounding character of the area and streetscape pattern. The proposal will result in a disruption to the established pattern of development, character of the surrounding plots, and built form of the area. The proposal will would be materially and detrimentally harmful to the appearance and character of the&nbsp;surrounding area and sit at odds with the existing character.&nbsp;&nbsp;As such, the proposed development is contrary to:- National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)- Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)- Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5&nbsp;of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037: (September 2024)",
    "&nbsp;The addition of a dwelling of this design, by reason of&nbsp;scale, siting and design would result in significantly impacting adjoining sites and neighbouring dwellings which would result in creating a sense of overbearing, overshadowing, loss of outlook, loss of daylight and an increase in coming and goings, noise, activity and potential disturbances to the site. This will result in causing undue harm to adjoining and surrounding residents, as such, therefore constituting unneighbourly development and contrary to:- National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)- Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021);- Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5&nbsp;of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037: (September, 2024)",
    "The application has failed to provide sufficient information regarding the proposed off-street car parking arrangement and may further increase the existing parking stress in the area. This is considered to be unacceptable and contrary to: - Paragraph 116 of the&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, December 2024)- Policy T6 of the London Plan (March 2021)- Policy DMT 3 of the&nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s&nbsp;Local Plan 2037(September 2024)",
    "In the absence of information demonstrating the Small Site Metric calculations in full, the proposal fails to demonstrate compliance with the Biodiversity Net Gain Requirements and is contrary to Schedule 7A of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990.&amp;nbsp;"
  ],
